[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-98689"] :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t],$ the vector space of real polynomials of degree at most $2,$ and let the inner product on $V$ be defined as\n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1).\n$$\n\nNow consider the following elements of $V:$\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)={t}^{2}-t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)={t}^{2}+t,\\,q(t)=4{t}^{2}-t-1\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $S=\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ given that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the inner product, and that the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t)}$ equals $2{t}^{2}-2t.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,q(t)={\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t).\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)=2{t}^{2}-2t,$ so let's now find the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{p}_{2}(t)}.$ This can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t)=\\frac{⟨q(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩}{⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩}\\,{p}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨q(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =q(-1){p}_{2}(-1)+q(0){p}_{2}(0)+q(1){p}_{2}(1) \\\\  & =(4{t}^{2}\\,-\\,t\\,-\\,1){|}_{-1}\\,\\,\\cdot \\,({t}^{2}\\,+\\,t){|}_{-1}+(4{t}^{2}\\,-\\,t\\,-\\,1){|}_{0}\\,\\,\\cdot \\,({t}^{2}\\,+\\,t){|}_{0}+(4{t}^{2}\\,-\\,t\\,-\\,1){|}_{1}\\,\\,\\cdot \\,({t}^{2}\\,+\\,t){|}_{1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & ={p}_{2}(-1){p}_{2}(-1)+{p}_{2}(0){p}_{2}(0)+{p}_{2}(1){p}_{2}(1) \\\\  & =({t}^{2}+t)^{2}{|}_{-1}+({t}^{2}+t)^{2}{|}_{0}+({t}^{2}+t)^{2}{|}_{1} \\\\  & ={0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t) & =\\frac{4}{4}\\cdot ({t}^{2}+t)={t}^{2}+t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,q(t) & ={\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t) \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}-2t+({t}^{2}+t) \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-105219/selection/cbccd6bc9a6b618df69da9a61720becfb162d5f1a71fff7d9362d3623bf4e2e7" :answer/id #uuid "147561c7-14e4-508e-a5dd-cbee2d129aed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105219/selection/60ab4b9fac5cd7f3eeee6fe1c4ac4dadf3c7b2cb23d0994c4225b376b8bdb435" :answer/id #uuid "6b190447-c8cc-53ba-a39e-869dd35a2752" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105219/selection/adea6de6de33b77366fb56ce5e7c5bea8e168241aa8eb80c0701b0fec906ee66" :answer/id #uuid "0cce0153-36f5-560a-90f5-1f3f35269b1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105219/selection/0a5121f80fb621886a1449cec13265bd0403c410d774eda967c89cfa676a6a1b" :answer/id #uuid "41ff7c3b-ff01-569e-bc92-5e757efff761" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105219/selection/5ec025638ddbdef47ebd8695170681ed171c149f49e40e41a8e660982f3f3131" :answer/id #uuid "ae899bdb-3836-5da7-856c-855a176f5abf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105219/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b1286aba-efef-5fe2-97da-4e03cd0da572" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105219/selection/0a5121f80fb621886a1449cec13265bd0403c410d774eda967c89cfa676a6a1b" :answer-field/choices ["q-105219/selection/cbccd6bc9a6b618df69da9a61720becfb162d5f1a71fff7d9362d3623bf4e2e7" "q-105219/selection/60ab4b9fac5cd7f3eeee6fe1c4ac4dadf3c7b2cb23d0994c4225b376b8bdb435" "q-105219/selection/adea6de6de33b77366fb56ce5e7c5bea8e168241aa8eb80c0701b0fec906ee66" "q-105219/selection/0a5121f80fb621886a1449cec13265bd0403c410d774eda967c89cfa676a6a1b" "q-105219/selection/5ec025638ddbdef47ebd8695170681ed171c149f49e40e41a8e660982f3f3131"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105219" :question/id #uuid "d54a1f9d-2365-54c2-8a4e-cb77c343af4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-105219" :question/problem "Let $V=C[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the vector space of continuous functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$, and let the inner product on $V$ be defined as\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNow consider the following elements of $V:$\n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(t)=1,\\,{f}_{2}(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,g(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $S=\\text{Span}{{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)}$ given that ${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the inner product, and that the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{f}_{2}(t)}$ equals $-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,g(t)={\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t).\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t)=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,$ so let's now find the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{f}_{1}(t)}.$ This can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)=\\frac{⟨g(t),{f}_{1}(t)⟩}{⟨{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{1}(t)⟩}\\,{f}_{1}(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨g(t),{f}_{1}(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(t){f}_{1}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+3t]_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(2-0+3\\pi )-(2-0-3\\pi ) \\\\  & =6\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{1}(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }1\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t) & =\\frac{6\\pi }{2\\pi }\\cdot 1=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,g(t) & ={\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t) \\\\  & =3-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-105219/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "39692b40-7d68-5ae5-9fe1-0f8b0b2e0d77"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105219"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105496/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "3c03425b-e8c6-5e76-b608-573ae3e46d22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105496/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "8c3accac-fdf3-5750-b0b8-a663f8235898" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105496/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "f84b4bb4-3104-5dfc-b7a5-1c6691c1287c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105496/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "667a123d-774c-54e8-b69f-4fde26874f4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105496/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "f901e143-9b26-575a-9f23-13f61cad5cd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105496/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a39d2211-f1c8-5cd4-88a1-1a597eefbe6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105496/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-105496/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" "q-105496/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-105496/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-105496/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-105496/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105496" :question/id #uuid "49ea9adf-d0b5-5c27-8ee7-8550fea7b78d" :question/math-academy-id "q-105496" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{1}[t],$ the vector space of polynomials of degree at most $1$ with real coefficients. Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nfind the distance between $f(t)=8t-3$ and $g(t)=3t+2$ with respect to the inner product." :question/worked-solution "The distance between $f(t)=8t-3$ and $g(t)=3t+2$ with respect to the given inner product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =‖f(t)-g(t)‖ \\\\  & =‖8t-3-(3t+2)‖ \\\\  & =‖5t-5‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{⟨5t-5,5t-5⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨5t-5,5t-5⟩ & =(5t-5){|}_{0}\\cdot (5t-5){|}_{0}+(5t-5){|}_{1}\\cdot (5t-5){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot (-5)+0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance is $d=\\sqrt{25}=5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-105496/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "25e84fac-02c3-5111-98b3-bc67fe1ec9ab"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105496"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105498/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "49d03d3a-2ac9-5356-8408-fb1db1397d31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105498/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "c47b3581-fcfd-50d9-8732-73c1b5d74519" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105498/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "f40919de-53f8-509e-bc1c-8df81c5c6595" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105498/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "9b049f8d-848c-5010-b4f8-ed95bb4e83eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105498/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "ef271ddb-b2c5-52d6-b348-3ccc87d625c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105498/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "56bab4cc-154d-51a6-bdf3-616675e7c579" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105498/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-105498/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-105498/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-105498/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-105498/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-105498/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105498" :question/id #uuid "f12a29fb-7c8e-5ef7-b086-14df38ba86c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-105498" :question/problem "Let $V=C[0,1],$ the vector space of functions that are continuous over $[0,1].$ Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nfind the distance between $f(t)=8t-3$ and $g(t)=2t-1$ with respect to the inner product." :question/worked-solution "The distance between $f(t)=8t-3$ and $g(t)=2t-1$ with respect to the given inner product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =‖f(t)-g(t)‖ \\\\  & =‖8t-3-(2t-1)‖ \\\\  & =‖6t-2‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{⟨6t-2,6t-2⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨6t-2,6t-2⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(6t-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(36{t}^{2}-24t+4)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[12{t}^{3}-12{t}^{2}+4t]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(12-12+4)-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance is $d=\\sqrt{4}=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-105498/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "25e84fac-02c3-5111-98b3-bc67fe1ec9ab"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105498"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
